Z||000002||FieroLisa||05-12-2001||01:36 AM||||I had that problem with my coupe twice- first time it was when I first bought the coupe and it needed a new transmission, because it was spewing little metal shards out. So that ran me $1,100. Then about a year and a half later it started at it again, and I just sent it to my mechanic in frustration. Even though he took forever figuring it out, and told me he had to take out the tranny 3 times, apparently he got it fixed.<P>I bought my GT sight unseen from across the country, so I had a mechanic check it out- he said it was hard going into 2nd and 4th but fixed the transmission linkage and I never had any problem with it. But occaisionally when I go on long highway drives and I get into traffic and need to take it into 2nd or 1st it will take some time to get her shifting right again. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/daytona1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
